mmc: rda: never sleep under priv->lock

Root cause of the intermittent total system freeze, caught red-handed by
lockdep + DEBUG_ATOMIC_SLEEP on the bench:

  BUG: sleeping function called from invalid context at rda-mmc.c:170
  ...
  BUG: spinlock cpu recursion on CPU#0, irq/23-mmc0
   lock: ... .owner: kworker/0:2/38

rda_mmc_request() held priv->lock (spin_lock_irqsave) across the whole
command execution, and the command path sleeps in readl_poll_timeout /
usleep_range. When the mmc irq thread contended the lock while its owner
was scheduled out mid-sleep, the UP system deadlocked silently — the
"random" freeze during card init and sustained I/O.

Fix: priv->lock now only guards the priv->mrq handoff. The command path
runs unlocked; the irq thread and the request-timeout path race for
ownership via the mrq claim (both re-check after locking). Also hoist
clk_get_rate() (takes a mutex) out of the locked section in set_ios.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local fix of a backported not-yet-merged series]

Signed-off-by: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
---

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/rda-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/rda-mmc.c
